"Lee County Elections, FL | Official Website (https://www.lee.vote/)\nciteturn5view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.lee.vote/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: ###\nL1: \nL2: cite0†Skip to Main Content L3: \nL4: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Important Notice cite2†Vote-by-Mail Request Renewal Required Read More... L7: \nL8: cite3†Image L9: \nL10: [Input: Search...] Search\nL11: \nL12: Active Registered Voters:\nL13: \nL14: Democrats:\nL15: \nL16: Republicans:\nL17: \nL18: Other:\nL19: \nL20: Total:\nL21: \nL22:   * cite4†Back to Home L23: \nL24:   * cite5†Register to Vote L25: \nL26:   * cite6†Vote By Mail L27: \nL28:   * cite7†Update My Voter Record L29: \nL30:   * cite8†Where Do I Vote L31: \nL32:   * cite8†Check My Voter Record L33: \nL34: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL35: ### Important Information\nL36: \nL37:   1. # Vote-by-Mail Request Renewal Required\nL38: \nL39: The deadline to request a Vote-by-Mail ballot for the November 3, 2026, General Election is 5:00 pm, Thursday, October 22.\nL40: \nL41: Under Florida law, all previous Vote-by-Mail requests have expired. You must cite9†submit a new request to vote by mail in the 2026 election cycle.\nL42: \nL43:   2. # Early Voting Information\nL44: \nL45: For early voting information, including hours, locations, and wait times, cite10†visit our Early Voting Information page .\nL46:   3. # Sample Ballots for the 2026 General Election\nL47: \nL48: Sample ballots for the November 3, 2026, General Election are now available.\nL49: cite11†Find your voter-specific Sample Ballot L50: \nL51: cite12†View the all-inclusive Sample Ballot L52: \nL53: Important Note\nL54:      * Town of Fort Myers Beach Town Council candidate John McLean has withdrawn from the race. Due to the late withdrawal, his name will still appear on the ballot. Any votes for balloted, withdrawn candidates will be tallied but will not count.\nL55:      * Gateway Services Community Development District Seat 4 candidate Paul LeoGrande has withdrawn from the race. Due to the late withdrawal, the candidate's name and contest will still appear on the ballot. A vote cast in the Gateway Services Community Development District Seat 4 race will not change the outcome, as the remaining candidate is deemed by law to be unopposed and elected for that race. All votes cast in this race will be tallied but will not count.\nL56:   4. # Current Election Statistics\nL57: cite13†View a breakdown of ballots cast for an upcoming election. L58: \nL59: On election night, Tuesday, November 3, we will release and post preliminary, unofficial local election results shortly after 7:00 p.m. The 1st unofficial results, 2nd unofficial results (only for recounts), and official results will be compiled on the dates designated by the Canvassing Board Meetings and Logic and Accuracy Testing Schedule\nL60: \nL61:   5. # Updating your Florida Driver's License or ID Card Number\nL62: Have you recently updated or been issued a new Florida driver's license or ID card? Due to changes implemented to the numbering system by the Department of Highway Safety and Motor Vehicles (DHSMV), your new driver's license or identification card number may be different from the one on your voter registration record. I t’s important to update your voter registration information with your new number.\nL63: This identification number helps us verify your identity when processing your request for a vote-by-mail ballot or an address change.\nL64: To update your voter registration with your new Florida driver’s license or ID card number, you may:\nL65:      * Call us at (239) LEE-VOTE (533-8683)\nL66:      * Visit cite14†RegisterToVoteFlorida.gov†www.registertovoteflorida.gov to update your record.\nL67:      * Complete and submit a Florida Voter Registration Application\nL68:        * cite15†Florida Voter Registration Application (English PDF) L69:        * cite16†Florida Voter Registration Application (Spanish PDF) L70:      * Update your registration when you update your driver’s license or ID card at the DMV.\nL71: \nL72:   6. # Voter Registration Deadline\nL73: The deadline to register to vote for the November 3, 2026, General Election was Monday, October 5.\nL74: \nL75: For more information on registering to vote, cite17†visit our Voter Registration Information page .\nL76: \nL77:   7. # Congressional Redistricting\nL78: In 2026, the Florida Legislature passed House Bill 1D, which establishes new or revised congressional districts in several counties across the state. While Lee County’s voters remain in either Congressional District 17 or 19, your congressional district may have changed from 17 to 19 or vice versa under the new legislative map. Some voters will not experience a change in their congressional district.\nL79: \nL80: cite11†View your personalized voting information, including your Congressional District, here. L81:   8. # Subscribe to our Newsletter\nL82: \nL83: You can keep up with everything happening at Lee County Elections cite18†by reading our Quarterly Newsletter .\nL84: \nL85: Be sure to cite19†subscribe to our newsletter†vote.us15.list-manage.com so you don't miss anything!\nL86: \nL87:   9. # Online Service Tools\nL88: If you need assistance, you have the option to use our online service tools, which are available on this site and do not require an in-person visit to our office. On this site, you can cite17†register to vote , cite20†update your voter registration record , make or update a cite21†Vote-by-Mail ballot request , or cite22†contact us .\nL89: \nL90: Please call the office at (239) LEE-VOTE (533-8683) if you require information that is not available on this site or if you need assistance using one of our online service tools.\nL91: ### Follow Us\nL92: \nL93:   * 